    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required exposing an owner's `initials` \u2014 the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `J.S.`).\n\n`OwnerDto` is generated from the OpenAPI spec, and the read-only `displayName` field was already computed in `OwnerMapper`. I mirrored that existing pattern rather than introducing anything new:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` property to the `Owner` schema, alongside `displayName`, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"initials\", expression = \"java(initials(owner))\")` and a small `initials(Owner)` default method, factoring the per-name logic into a private `initial(String)` helper so the computation stays a single-responsibility unit next to the analogous `displayName`.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreComputesInitials` passes (`J.S.` for \"john\"/\"smith\"), and the full build is green.",
